  "details": "I’ve been having an issue when doing the custom rotations on the eye settings. \nIn the vrchat SDK, the eyes work as they should. \nBut in-game, the eyes are a bit wonky, sometimes moving further than the limit that was set in the SDK. But that can be fixed with a bit of tweaking.\nOne of my eyes has a limit that’s too small, so the eye for some reason cannot rotate past that point, even though in the SDK it looks fine. I can’t increase the rotation or anything, it seems that the eye just stops at that point no matter what the value is. Has anyone else had this problem before? \nI even disabled IK 2.0 because I know there’s been issues with it, but the eye still won’t rotate fully. I’m trying to make the eye look right. The other eye moves fully, but this specific eye just won’t.",
